<title>UK: Brazil's CSN to launch $300 mln bond soon-bankers.</title>
<headline>Brazil's CSN to launch $300 mln bond soon-bankers.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's CSN Iron SA plans to launch a $300 million 10-year Eurobond this week, bankers said on Monday.</p>
<p>CSN Iron is wholly owned and guaranteed by Companhia Siderurgica Nacional, the largest steel producer in Brazil.</p>
<p>The notes will be rated B1 by Moody's Investors Service, Moody's said last week. J.P. Morgan will underwrite the issue.</p>
<p>&quot;CSN is expected to be launched on Tuesday,&quot; an emerging market Eurobond trader said.</p>
<p>Spread talk was between 270 and 290 basis points over U.S. Treasury notes, the trader said.</p>
<p>-- Aline van Duyn, London Newsroom +44 171</p>
</text>
